## Third-party material and share-alike (read before relying on CC BY 4.0)

This repository does not redistribute the four source datasets as datasets, and
it does not redistribute model weights. However, the frozen item list
`harness/data/core_prompt/items.jsonl` embeds the item text (questions,
SQuAD 2.0 passages, FEVER claims and evidence sentences, gold answers) of the
800 sampled instances, and the raw responses in `harness/results/` quote those
items in the prompt records.

Those excerpts remain under the licence of their source dataset, not CC BY 4.0.
Two of the four sources are **share-alike**:

  | Source        | Licence recorded on the dataset card | Share-alike |
  |---------------|--------------------------------------|-------------|
  | TruthfulQA    | Apache-2.0                           | no          |
  | SQuAD 2.0     | CC BY-SA 4.0                         | yes         |
  | FEVER         | CC BY-SA 3.0 (Wikipedia text)        | yes         |
  | KILT          | MIT (Wikipedia snapshot: CC BY-SA)   | yes, in part|

Consequences, to be settled before the archive is deposited (see
docs/DATA_SOURCES.md, "Open question"):

  1. Either keep the excerpts and license the affected files under CC BY-SA 4.0
     instead of CC BY 4.0, or
  2. deposit only the identifier-only item list
     (`harness/data/core_prompt/items.ids.jsonl`, which contains no source
     text) and let users rebuild the full list with
     `experiments/core_prompt/build_items.py`.

Verify each licence on the current dataset card before submission; the table
above records what the cards stated when this repository was assembled.
